# TypeScript standards

- `strict: true` — no `any`. Prefer precise types; shared types live in `@/shared/types`.
- Prefer `type` aliases for props and DTOs; narrow with type guards / filters instead of casts.
- Import cross-folder via `@/` only (e.g. `@/entities/menu/api`).
- Entity API: keep DTO types next to the API; map to model types when the UI needs a different shape.
- After non-trivial changes, leave the tree green: `pnpm lint` and `pnpm typecheck`.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
const item = nodes[id] as CatalogMenuItemDto;

// ✅ GOOD
.filter((item): item is CatalogMenuItemDto => item != null);
```
